Clustering Tool

DESCRIPTION:
This tool performs clustering analysis to identify groups, subpopulations, 
or patterns in biological or clinical data.

FUNCTIONALITY:
- Multiple clustering algorithms (K-means, Leiden, Hierarchical, DBSCAN)
- Automatic cluster number selection
- Cluster quality evaluation (silhouette score, etc.)
- Marker feature identification
- Visualization data generation

INPUT FORMAT:
1. data: 2D feature matrix (samples x features)
   - Rows are samples
   - Columns are features
   - Example: [[1.0, 2.0, 3.0], [1.1, 2.1, 3.1], ...]

2. algorithm: Clustering algorithm (default: "leiden")
   - Options: "kmeans", "leiden", "louvain", "hierarchical", "dbscan"

3. n_clusters: Number of clusters (optional for leiden/louvain)

4. resolution: Resolution parameter for leiden/louvain (default: 1.0)

OUTPUT FORMAT:
{
    "labels": [0, 0, 1, 1, 2, ...],
    "clusters": {
        "cluster_0": {"size": 10, "centroid": [...]},
        "cluster_1": {"size": 15, "centroid": [...]}
    },
    "quality_metrics": {
        "silhouette_score": 0.65,
        "inertia": 125.4
    },
    "graph": {
        "clusters": {...},
        "centroids": [...],
        "type": "cluster_graph"
    }
}

USAGE NOTES:
- Normalize data before clustering for best results
- K-means requires specifying n_clusters
- Leiden/Louvain automatically determine cluster count
- Use silhouette score to evaluate clustering quality

